def abstract(doc):
    heading(doc,'Abstract',1)
    p(doc,'Early-stage founders often make decisions about markets, costs, registration and launch activity using fragmented information, generic online advice and unstructured spreadsheets. This dissertation presents VentureMind AI, a web-based startup lifecycle management prototype that consolidates startup profiling, explainable risk assessment, financial planning, business registration guidance, advisor booking and launch-management tools in one local-first platform. The project was developed as a React and TypeScript single-page application supported by a FastAPI and Python REST API, SQLAlchemy, Alembic and MySQL. Role-based access is provided for founders, administrators and human advisors. The AI component combines a transparent deterministic risk engine with local large-language-model support through Ollama. This design intentionally separates repeatable scores from generated narrative so that a founder can inspect the evidence, scorecards, assumptions and recommended actions rather than treating an AI response as a guarantee of business success.\n\nThe development followed an iterative, risk-driven Agile approach. Requirements were translated into user journeys for founding a business: describe the venture, assess risks and competitors, create a financial forecast, complete business requirements, seek specialist advice, prepare registration activity and manage early launch operations. The resulting prototype demonstrates connected workflows and persistent records for projects, profiles, risk assessments, financial plans, reports, appointments and administrative tasks. Evaluation uses functional test cases, role-based scenario walkthroughs and quality criteria derived from ISO/IEC 25010. The study concludes that an explainable, workflow-oriented platform can make startup decision support more understandable and actionable. However, it does not replace customer research, professional legal advice, financial advice or official government registration systems. Future work should validate the risk model using longitudinal founder outcomes, introduce consented live data providers, and complete production-grade payment and social publishing integrations.')
    p(doc,'Keywords: startup lifecycle management; explainable artificial intelligence; decision support; risk assessment; FastAPI; React; Ollama; Sri Lanka.',italic=True)
    doc.add_page_break()

